# Loaded automatically by `vite build` (Vite's mode-specific env file
# convention — see .env.example for the dev-only counterpart). Committed,
# not git-ignored: nothing here is a secret.
#
# Intentionally empty: there is no mock mode, so there is no
# VITE_API_REAL_DOMAINS toggle to set anymore — every build always talks to
# the real backend. VITE_DEV_PROXY_TARGET is also not needed here: production
# serves the frontend from the same origin as the backend (nginx
# reverse-proxies /api/* — see frontend/README.md), so fetch('/api/...')
# already resolves correctly with no dev-proxy involved. This file exists so
# a future maintainer sees this note instead of wondering whether it was
# emptied by accident.
